        <item>
            <title>1.15.1</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:02:12 +0530</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>259</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.15.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
  <li>App Store updates of an open app now go through Keel&#x27;s usual step: the row asks Quit and Update or Skip, Keel quits the app itself, updates it and opens it again. The App Store no longer asks &quot;cannot be open during installation&quot; again and again.</li>
  <li>Keel also waits for an app&#x27;s own helper processes inside the app (such as WhatsApp&#x27;s ServiceExtension) and asks them to quit before the App Store installs.</li>
  <li>If an App Store update makes no progress for 10 minutes, Keel stops it; the row says the App Store is waiting for the app to quit and nothing was changed, with Update still there.</li>
  <li>&quot;User has cancelled install&quot; from the App Store now shows as Cancelled, not a failure, and other App Store errors show their plain description instead of a raw error dump.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
